# text = The puppy saw nothing incongruous in learning at the same time a ditty of love and a description of the plague Why , they are much the same thing So I told him , in excuse for his coxcombry -- but my youth stared me rebukingly in the face , without taking the jest , and answered , that it was only the insensate ear that the music pleased , whereas the book ( the description of the plague , mind you !) elevated the heart . " Ah !" quoth the fat uncle , wheezing , " my boy is quite an Athenian , always mixing the utile with the dulce ." O Minerva , how I laughed in my sleeve !
