# text = Imagine every entertainment for mind and body -- enumerate all the gymnastic games our fathers invented -- repeat all the books Italy and Greece have produced -- suppose places for all these games , admirers for all these works -- add to this , baths of the vastest size , the most complicated construction -- intersperse the whole with gardens , with theatres , with porticoes , with schools -- suppose , in one word , a city of the gods , composed but of palaces and public edifices , and you may form some faint idea of the glories of the great baths of Rome By Hercules why , it would take a man's whole life to bathe At Rome , it often does so There are many who live only at the baths .
