# text = From its jaws I hear a voice that summons us to ENJOY By Pollux the wine thou sellest us , old is enough to thin the best blood in one's veins None of thy scurrilous blusterings with me my wine is good enough for a carcass which shall so soon soak the dust of the spoliarium Croakest thou thus , old raven thou shalt live to hang thyself with despite when thou seest me win the palm crown ; and when I get the purse at the amphitheatre , as I certainly shall , my first vow to Hercules shall be to forswear thee and thy vile potations evermore Hear to him -- hear to this modest Pyrgopolinices !
