# text = The countryman of thy ancestors , the cave-nursed Plato , dreamed of such a love -- his followers have sought to imitate it ; but it is a love that is not for the herd to echo -- it is a love that only high and noble natures can conceive -- it hath nothing in common with the sympathies and ties of coarse affection -- wrinkles do not revolt it -- homeliness of feature does not deter ; it asks youth , it is true , but it asks it only in the freshness of the emotions ; it asks beauty , it is true , but it is the beauty of the thought and of the spirit .
