# text = There is but one such man in these places whom the men of the outer world , unknowing his loftier attributes and more secret fame , call Arbaces the Egyptian : to us of a higher nature and deeper knowledge , his rightful appellation is Hermes of the Burning Girdle I am he I have seen , then the Lord of the Mighty Girdle -- vouchsafe my homage Rise I have need of thee Thou sayest that thou art a daughter of the ancient Etrurian tribes ; the mighty walls of whose rock-built cities yet frown above the robber race that hath seized upon their ancient reign .
