# text = Yet , strange to say , he cannot account for the cause of the sudden frenzy that seized him -- he retains but a dim consciousness of what hath passed ; and , despite thy witness , wise Egyptian , solemnly upholds his innocence of the death of Apaecides Sallust there is much in thy friend's case that merits a peculiar indulgence ; and could we learn from his lips the confession and the cause of his crime , much might be yet hoped from the mercy of the senate ; for the senate , thou knowest , hath the power either to mitigate or to sharpen the law .
