# text = If anything can make me forget that I am an Athenian and not free , it is partly the soothing -- the love -- watchful , vivid , sleepless -- of Ione -- a love that has taken a new sentiment in our new creed -- a love which none of our poets , beautiful though they be , had shadowed forth in description ; for mingled with religion , it partakes of religion ; it is blended with pure and unworldly thoughts ; it is that which we may hope to carry through eternity , and keep , therefore , white and unsullied , that we may not blush to confess it to our God !
